{"name":"Schooner","hex":"#8d8478","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"schooner","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sailing ship with two or more masts, all with fore-and-aft sails; if two masted, having a foremast and a mainmast.","A glass for drinking a large measure of sherry."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/schooner"}],"entries":[{"title":"Schooner","blocks":[{"text":"A schooner is a type of sailing vessel defined by its fore-and-aft rig on all of two or more masts and the foremast generally being shorter than the mainmast. The most common variants are gaff-rigged and staysail schooners, with the topsail schooner carrying a square topsail on the foremast, and Bermuda and junk-rigs being rarities."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Lewis_R._French_NHL.jpg/330px-Lewis_R._French_NHL.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Schooner"},{"title":"Schooner (glass)","blocks":[{"text":"A schooner is a type of glass or a fluid measure for serving alcoholic drinks, which varies by country."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Geordie_Schooner.jpg/330px-Geordie_Schooner.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Schooner_(glass)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Oosterschelde_Kieler_Foerde.jpg/500px-Oosterschelde_Kieler_Foerde.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Oosterschelde_Kieler_Foerde.jpg/1280px-Oosterschelde_Kieler_Foerde.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Oosterschelde_Kieler_Foerde.jpg/500px-Oosterschelde_Kieler_Foerde.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parse